<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wenceslaus III of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1289">1289</a>–<a href="/years/1306">1306</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Ladislaus V of Hungary · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wenceslaus III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1301 to 1305, as Ladislaus V, and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1305–1306. Son of Wenceslaus II, he was elected in Hungary after the extinction of the Árpád dynasty but lost ground to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-hungary">Charles Robert of Anjou</a> and handed his claim to Otto of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. His murder at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> in 1306 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/premyslid-dynasty">Přemyslid dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wenceslaus-iii-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Wenceslaus III of Bohemia" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Szilágyi Sándor · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaclav3_pecet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Charles Robert of Anjou, a descendant through the female line, <b>Wenceslaus of Bohemia</b> and Otto of Bavaria all claimed the throne.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1000-1301">Kingdom of Hungary (1000-1301) · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Charles Robert of Anjou, grandson of Mary of Hungary, a daughter of Stephen V, was backed by the papacy but opposed first by <b>Wenceslaus of Bohemia</b>, crowned in 1301, and then by Otto of Bavaria, crowned in 1305.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/czech-republic">the Czech Republic</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/czech-republic">the Czech Republic</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50.09,14.42&amp;year=1300" aria-label="Prague on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4880 422 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Wenceslaus III of Bohemia"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5330 692h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5330 692h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50.09,14.42&amp;year=1300">What was here in 1300? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
